                "senderName": "NWS Tampa Bay Ruskin FL",
                "headline": "Flood Warning issued September 18 at 8:56PM EDT by NWS Tampa Bay Ruskin FL",
                "description": "...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Florida...\n\nWithlacoochee At US 41 Dunnellon affecting Citrus, Levy and Marion\nCounties.\n\n.The Withlacoochee River at Dunnellon has been steadily rising since\nJuly, and on September 15 reached flood stage. The cause of the high\nwater along the Withlacoochee River at Dunnellon is due to excessive\nhydrilla growth (from the river bottom to the water surface) along a\n4.5 mile stretch of river between US 41 and Lake Rousseau.  The\nhydrilla is acting like a dam and holding water back, causing water\nlevels to rise.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Withlacoochee at US 41 Dunnellon.\n\n* WHEN...Until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 28.2 feet, Docks and boat ramps flood along the river\nin Citrus and Marion counties.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 7:45 PM EDT Friday the stage was 28.2 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 28.2 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to remain above flood stage\nuntil further notice.\n- Flood stage is 28.2 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 28.2\nfeet on 10/02/1979.\n- https://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Saturday afternoon at noon EDT.",
                "response": "Avoid",
